    "evenflo_faq_NWMprn": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_QX7qXH": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How long will my Shyft™ DualRide™ last?",
            "content": "<p>The Evenflo Shyft™  DualRide™ has a 6-year expiration from the date of manufacture. The specific expiration date is listed on the date and model label on the product.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_XMUaFR": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Where is the date and model label?",
            "content": "<p>You can find the date of manufacture, model name, and model number on two labels on the Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™. One is found on the underside of the infant carrier. The second label is on the underside of the base.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_CyBzwT": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How much does the Shyft™ DualRide™ weigh?",
            "content": "<p>The Shyft™ DualRide™ weighs a total of 28 lb (12.7 kg) with all the components combined, including the infant carrier, stroller frame, and base. In stroller mode, or in carrier mode with the stroller frame attached, the product weighs approximately 19 lb (8.6 kg). When used as an infant carrier without the stroller frame, the product weighs approximately 8 lb (3.6 kg)</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_mHeLwe": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Is the Shyft™ DualRide™ heavier than other infant car seats?",
            "content": "<p>The Shyft™ DualRide™ is a little bit heavier than most infant car seats — but for a good reason! It’s designed to function as a one-piece combo: an infant car seat that opens into a stroller with the wheels and frame already attached. After removing from the base, just squeeze the release on the infant car seat and the stroller wheels drop down, which makes transitioning from the backseat of your vehicle to the sidewalk or driveway seamless. Thanks to this integrated stroller system, you won’t need to carry the infant car seat often. However, the Shyft™ DualRide™ may also be removed from the base without the stroller frame attached, for a lightweight carry option.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_nrwNXh": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What are the dimensions of the Shyft™ DualRide™ in stroller mode?",
            "content": "<p>35” d (88.9 cm) x 41.5” h (105.4 cm) x 18” w (45.7 cm)</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_TN4myC": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Where is my Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ user guide stored on the product?",
            "content": "<p>The user guide for the Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ can be stored on top of the stroller frame, underneath the infant car seat. It is a good idea to always keep your user guide with your car seat so you can refer to this information as needed. Additionally, you may find an electronic copy of your user guide on our website at www.evenflo.com.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
