    "evenflo_faq_xYfNee": {
      "type": "evenflo-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_MqLjCU": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "What standards does this car seat meet?",
            "content": "<p>The Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ meets or exceeds all applicable Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standards (FMVSS) and Canadian Motor Vehicle Safety Standards (CMVSS). In addition, this infant car seat meets the Consumer Product Safety Commission standard for handheld infant carriers.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_AqRGCR": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "Is this car seat JPMA Certified?",
            "content": "<p>The Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ meets the Juvenile Product Manufacturer’s Association (JPMA) certification for handheld infant carriers.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_xUxnPm": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "If car seats are required by government regulation to be flame-retardant, how does Evenflo make sure it meets the government standard?",
            "content": "<p>Flammability testing of car seats is required under the FMVSS 302, Flammability of Interior Materials Standard. The test measures the rate of flame spread with the goal of maximizing the amount of time a caregiver would have to remove an occupant from the car seat in the event of a vehicle fire. Evenflo’s car seats are tested by an accredited independent testing laboratory and meet the FMVSS 302 standard. In addition, Evenflo car seats are tested for toxicity to meet or exceed the regulations of various state and federal child products banned substances laws and regulations.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_Vfra6e": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "How is this car seat tested?",
            "content": "<p>At Evenflo, we go above and beyond government standards to create car seats that are safe. The Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ meets or exceeds all applicable federal safety standards. It is structural integrity tested at energy levels approximately 2x the federal crash test standard, additionally, it is side impact tested, rollover tested, and temperature tested.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_XY7VU6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "checkbox_expanded": false,
            "title": "I live in Canada. Can I buy an Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ in the USA and use it in Canada?",
            "content": "<p>The Evenflo Shyft™ DualRide™ sold in the US may not comply with all Canadian regulatory requirements and, for that reason, does not have the required Maple Leaf label. You should always purchase a car seat that is compliant to the standards of the country in which you live. If you live in Canada, you must use a car seat that is compliant to the Canadian Motor Vehicle Safety Standards and has the Maple Leaf label.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
